{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"DISAMBIGUATION — two earlier comments on this ticket reference a bare 4-char id `00da`, which is AMBIGUOUS in this store and makes the resolver error during close-path text scans:\n\n  00da-1bda-d59c-4c2e  in_progress  rebar comment silently stores a flag-looking argument as the body\n  00da-b1af-89d4-4c47  closed       IR-to-BPMN serializer and rebar moddle extension\n\nBoth prior references mean **00da-1bda-d59c-4c2e** (the `rebar comment` body-handling bug). Context\nconfirms it: the sentences concern running `review-plan` on a never-reviewed ticket and overlap-judge\ncandidate neighbours during this epic's work, which is that ticket, not the BPMN serializer.\n\nA 4-char short id is NOT guaranteed unique. Use the full id or the user-friendly alias in ticket text.\nThe two comments cannot be edited (events are append-only), so this comment is the disambiguation of\nrecord."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785696538993088001,"uuid":"525d8e7e-ab07-4398-bdeb-97e52d73e19b"}